<ontology/use_varnish_paint_lacquer/use_varnish_paint_lacquer__1216__q2/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 212" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/dictionaryprac00mccu/page/n212/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Naphtha used in Varnish, Paint & Lacquer: McCulloch (1880), Dictionary of Commerce, scan p. 212"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "With certain vegetable oils, naphtha is said to form a good varnish.—2. Petroleum is much thicker than naphtha, resembling in consistence common tar."@en ;
